0.005 Tc
(Abstract)Tj
/F9 1 Tf
4.764 0 TD
-0.125 Tw
(Using a digital single lens reflex \(DSLR\) camera, I observed a transit)Tj
-4.764 -1.2 TD
-0.107 Tw
(of exoplanet HD 189733 in order to determine the feasibility of using these types)Tj
T*
-0.118 Tw
(of cameras for high-precision photometry. The results were scientifically useful,)Tj
T*
0.05 Tw
(showing that even though the camera is not explicitly designed for scientific)Tj
T*
-0.022 Tw
(applications, it can nevertheless produce high-quality differential photometry.)Tj
/F8 1 Tf
0 -2.4 TD
-0.018 Tc
-0.125 Tw
(1. Introduction)Tj
/F9 1 Tf
1.572 -2.4 TD
0.005 Tc
-0.042 Tw
(DSLR cameras have revolutionized amateur astroimaging, but they are not)Tj
-1.572 -1.2 TD
-0.081 Tw
(optimized for photometry and present a variety of obstacles for obtaining useful)Tj
T*
0.009 Tw
(data. First, DSLRs generally have a maximum bit depth of just 12 bits, which)Tj
T*
0 Tc
-0.125 Tw
(increases the risk of quantization errors caused by having relatively few steps with)Tj
T*
0.005 Tc
-0.057 Tw
(which to represent the dynamic range of an image. These errors can prevent the)Tj
T*
-0.005 Tw
(detection of subtle variations in the flux of a star. Second, the sensors in these)Tj
T*
0.001 Tc
-0.125 Tw
(cameras are overlaid with a matrix of color filters. This is particularly problematic)Tj
T*
0.005 Tc
-0.115 Tw
(because even though DSLRs have sensors with millions of pixels, only a fraction)Tj
T*
-0.125 Tw
(of those pixels will be covered by a particular color filter. In most cameras, half of)Tj
T*
-0.121 Tw
(the sensor\222s pixels are overlaid with green filters, one quarter with red filters, and)Tj
T*
0.125 Tw
(the remaining quarter with blue filters. Thus, there are non-negligible gaps)Tj
T*
0.004 Tc
-0.125 Tw
(between pixels of a given color, which can create spurious features in light curves)Tj
T*
-0.003 Tc
(as star images drift over different-colored pixels. Third, DSLRs have low quantum)Tj
T*
0.005 Tc
-0.04 Tw
(efficiency, making them ill-suited for faint objects, and anti-blooming sensors,)Tj
T*
-0.038 Tw
(which can compromise the linearity of the camera\222s response.)Tj
1.572 -1.2 TD
-0.104 Tw
(This paper assesses the photometric capabilities of DSLRs by presenting the)Tj
-1.572 -1.2 TD
0.003 Tc
-0.125 Tw
(results of an observation of an exoplanet transit with a DSLR. I first verify that my)Tj
T*
0.005 Tc
(DSLR\222s response curve is sufficiently linear for photometry before I describe the)Tj
T*
0.028 Tw
(procedures that I used to successfully observe an exoplanet transit.)Tj
/F8 1 Tf
0 -2.4 TD
-0.002 Tc
-0.125 Tw
(2. Overcoming DSLR limitations)Tj
/F9 1 Tf
1.572 -2.4 TD
0.005 Tc
-0.108 Tw
(As serious as the aforementioned limitations are, they do not prevent DSLRs)Tj
-1.572 -1.2 TD
-0.044 Tw
(from realizing a high level of photometric precision. The camera must be set to)Tj
T*
-0.104 Tw
(record images in its RAW mode, which, as its name implies, saves the raw image)Tj
T*
-0.122 Tw
(data without applying any form of processing. Consequently, it preserves the full)Tj
T*
0.001 Tc
-0.125 Tw
(12-bit data from each pixel without compromising the data\222s photometric quality.)Tj
ET
